  "why_graph": "Q6/Q7 walk variable-length PARENT_OF + RETRIEVED_FROM + MENTIONS paths and apply an ALL() wall-clock predicate over nodes(path); Q6 then continues through the advisory's public identity chain (HAS_ALIAS*0..1 -> REFERENCES*0..1) using the same Alias/Ref keys as the full OSV graph, so realized path lengths vary with the real alias/reference data. Q8 joins the answer's natural-language declaration with the lockfile pin and the advisory timeline, and resolves CVE/PYSEC aliases in the same query. A manifest-only scanner reads only PINS, so it reports clean while the stale declaration would still reach the next agent that reads the PR text."
